    "Practice Problem 1.2"

    A car company wants to improve their engine by 4x.
    Only 90% of the engine can be improved.
    How much would you need to improve that part to meet the target?

# ┗━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┛


###############
   "Answers"
###############

Answer: They will need to improve that part by 6x

Work:

  Told / Tnew
  1 / 4
  .25 * 1 = .25
  S = 4

  a = .9

  k = a / (1/S - (1 - a)	# See p01-1 for refactor info

  k = .9 / (1 / S - (1 - .9))
  k = .9 / (1 / S - (1 - .9))
  k = .9 / (1 / S - .1

  k = .9 / (1 / 4 - (1 - .9))
  k = .9 / (1 / 4 - (1 - .9))
  k = .9 / (1 / 4 - .1)
  k = .9 / (.25 - .1)
  k = .9 / .15
  k = 6


Sanity Check:

  S = 1 / ((1 - a) + a/k)

  S = 1 / ((1 - .9) + .9 / 6)
  S = 1 / ((.1) + .15)
  S = 1 / .25
  S = 4
